# Most turns of the loop run no other code; the turn that meets an escape calls, and comes round. The loop is built twice. The call stands IN the typed build: its way comes round through the front of quiet turns,
# which reads `end` anew and asks it for an int32 again; where that fails the loop goes on in its other build. `at`, which every turn reads and stores, is a parameter of the head and of the front.
# RUN: walk f4 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: [[entry]](v{{*}}) frequency=Rare:
# CHECK: [[head]]({{*}}i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: [[front]]({{*}}i32 @Int32) isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true:
# CHECK: = GetEnvironmentField
# CHECK: = TypeTest
# CHECK: [[leaves]]() frequency=Rare isInLoop=true:
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump -> next [[entry]](
# CHECK: Jump -> next [[head]](
# CHECK: = CallDirect {{*}}function=f3
# CHECK: Jump -> next [[front]](
# No quiet turn appends to `result`: every append stands in a turn that leaves the loop or calls. So the text lies in no string builder, which would forbid the second build.
# RUN(TEXT): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# TEXT-NOT: StringBuilder
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell
# ANSWERS: ab<n>cd<t>ef 2:12
